{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I will set apart on that day.</b> The earlier plagues were continuous; there would have been nothing so wondrous if they had been in the land of Egypt but not in the land of Goshen. But the plague of ערוב was a plague sent forth, and when it comes from the desert by the decree of El to uproot everything, it should naturally have come even to the land of Goshen, for it is part of the land of Egypt — except that the Holy One, blessed be He, set them apart by way of miracle and wonder for Israel's sake. And of this he said, <b>which my people stand upon it.</b> That is: because my people stand upon it." "<b>That you may know that I am YHWH in the midst of the earth.</b> Ruling and overseeing in the midst of the earth, to destroy the rebels and to save those who trust in Him. And he said this against Pharaoh the wicked, who denied providence and was of the sect that says (Job 22): ״עבים סתר לו ולא יראה וחוג שמים יתהלך״." "<b>And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote:</b> כי אני ה׳ בקרב הארץ — it is possible that it is like כי שמי בקרבו, and it is a lofty and hidden secret. End of quotation."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:05.588853459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}